# Where the server reads pipeline artifacts (manifest.json, ports.geojson, rasters, grids).
# Default: /data/v1, i.e. public/data/v1 written by `npm run data:live`.
# Production example (artifacts published by .github/workflows/coastwatch-data.yml):
# CW_DATA_BASE_URL=https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yashnil/habs-forecast/coastwatch-data/v1
CW_DATA_BASE_URL=/data/v1

# Optional: read artifacts from an absolute local directory instead (tests, debugging).
# CW_DATA_DIR=/absolute/path/to/v1

# --- Neritic private pilot: accounts, alerts, notifications (docs/coastwatch/pilot/accounts.md) ---
# Leave all of these unset and accounts/alerts work on the device only ("Not yet connected").
# Supabase project (us-west-1). The anon key is public by design (row-level security protects rows).
# A 127.0.0.1/localhost URL (the local stack) is labelled "Pilot demo"; a cloud URL is "Live".
# NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL=https://<project-ref>.supabase.co
# NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=<anon key>
# Server only, never NEXT_PUBLIC: used by /api/alerts/fanout to write inbox alerts.
# SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY=<service role key>
# Shared secret pg_cron sends as "Authorization: Bearer <secret>" to /api/alerts/fanout.
# ALERTS_FANOUT_SECRET=<long random string, e.g. openssl rand -hex 32>
# Web push (VAPID). Generate once: npx web-push@3.6.7 generate-vapid-keys
# NEXT_PUBLIC_VAPID_PUBLIC_KEY=<public key>
# VAPID_PRIVATE_KEY=<private key, server only>
# VAPID_SUBJECT=mailto:<owner contact>
# Absolute site URL used in notification links (also used for metadata).
# CW_SITE_URL=https://<private preview URL>
